<style>
  .legal { width: 560px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .legal ol { counter-reset: clause; list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 0; }
  .legal ol ol { padding-left: 26px; }
  .legal li { counter-increment: clause; margin: 5px 0; }
  .legal li::before { content: counters(clause, ".") ". "; font-weight: 700; color: #ff6b35; }
  .legal .h { font-weight: 700; }
</style>
<div class="card pad legal">
  <div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800">Terms of Messaging</div>
  <div class="tiny muted" style="margin-bottom: 8px">Nested numbering is generated by CSS <code>counters(clause, ".")</code> — no numbers in the HTML</div>
  <ol>
    <li><span class="h">Definitions.</span> In these terms, “Message” means any HTML document sent through the service, and “Bubble” means its rendered representation.
      <ol>
        <li>A Message may contain markup, inline styles and style blocks.</li>
        <li>A Message may not contain executable code; any such code is ignored.
          <ol>
            <li>This includes <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> elements and event-handler attributes.</li>
            <li>It also includes <code>javascript:</code> links, which are treated as ordinary text.</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
        <li>“Interactive state” means the set of keys toggled by <code>chat:</code> links.</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li><span class="h">Rendering.</span> Each Message is laid out independently.
      <ol>
        <li>Styles declared in one Message shall not affect any other Message.</li>
        <li>Bubbles shrink to the natural width of their content, up to a maximum width.</li>
        <li>Content wider than the maximum width is clipped at the Bubble edge.</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li><span class="h">Images.</span> Only images available synchronously are displayed.
      <ol>
        <li>Permitted sources are <code>data:</code> and <code>icon:</code>.</li>
        <li>Remote images are not fetched in this version.</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
    <li><span class="h">Miscellaneous.</span> If any clause is found unenforceable, the remaining clauses continue to render.
      <ol>
        <li>Headings in these terms are for convenience only.</li>
        <li>These terms are themselves a Message and are bound by them.</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>

